{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And all the people shall answer and say.</b> It did not suffice to say ״וְאָמַר כָל הָעָם״ in the manner it says regarding all the curses stated in the matter. The first one alerted [us] that Israel must respond to this — not that the Levites need to say ״וְאָמַר כָּל הָעָם״; rather, it is the verse's language that commands that the people shall answer and say amen, and there is nothing upon the Levites to say ״וְאָמַר כָל הָעָם״ etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:20.892431151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}